===Preposition===
{{en-head|prep}}

# {{lb|en|sometimes|proscribed}} [[after|After]], [[subsequent]] to.
#: {{ant|en|before|prior to}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Following''' the meeting, we all had a chat.}}
#: {{ux|en|We published our findings '''following''' a thorough review of others' earlier reports.}}
# [[in accordance with|In accordance with]]; [[as per]].
#: {{syn|en|per#Preposition}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Following''' all relevant safety instructions, administer a dose of the corticosteroid.}}
#: {{ux|en|Administer a dose of the corticosteroid, '''following''' all relevant safety instructions.}}

====Usage notes====
Among usage [[maven]]s,<!--e.g., not only Strunk and White but also many others--> there is a long tradition of [[deprecate|deprecating]] ''following'' (in its "after" sense) in favor of ''[[after]]'', coordinate with the long tradition of deprecating ''[[prior to]]'' in favor of ''[[before]]''; the rationale is avoiding [[puffery]] via (as some mavens call them) [[fancy]] words where [[plain]] ones would be better. However, there is an equally long tradition of writers not knowing of, caring about, or bothering with these [[Appendix:Glossary#prescriptive|prescriptions]], as well as an enduring urge to use fancy words to try to sound formal and authoritative<!--i.e., to succeed at wielding the [apparent] [[shibboleth]]s of [[book-learning]] or [[officialese]]-->.

